---
import ResidenceLayout from "../../../layouts/ResidenceLayout.astro";
import { frederick, frederickPhotos } from "../../../data/residences/frederick";
---

<ResidenceLayout
  residence={frederick}
  title="Utilities & systems · Frederick Cottage | Mt Cottages"
  description="Frederick Cottage utilities, trash and recycling, property systems, and maintenance paths — with honest confirmation steps."
  eyebrow="Frederick Cottage · Utilities"
  heading="How the house operates."
  lede="Heat, power, water, trash, internet, laundry, and who to call — organized so nothing needs a basic follow-up question after reading."
  hero={frederickPhotos.exteriorFrontSnow}
>
  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="site-width prose">
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Utilities</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>Extended stays include the home's core utilities under the arrangement — but provider names, thermostat type, and arrangement-specific inclusions are confirmed per stay, not published as permanent fact.</p>
          <ul><li>Heating/cooling, power, and water: included per the rental arrangement; confirm the current guide in the inquiry.</li><li>Internet: 1 Gbps ethernet hookups plus wifi — flag it early if remote work depends on a wired setup.</li><li>Laundry: washer and dryer are part of the amenity baseline; confirm location and supplies.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Trash & recycling</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>Marietta collection days, cart placement, and recycling rules are house-specific operational facts. This page will carry the schedule once confirmed.</p>
          <ul><li>Until then: ask for pickup day, cart location, and recycling sorting in the pre-arrival message.</li><li>Keep the entry, lawn, and carts tidy — the residential street sets the standard.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Property systems & maintenance</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>For non-emergency issues during a stay: describe the home, location, problem, timing, and photos only when they help — via the maintenance path. For immediate danger (fire, active gas smell, major flooding): call 911 first, then resident support.</p>
          <div class="cluster"><a class="button button--ghost" href="/maintenance.html">Maintenance path</a><a class="text-link" href="/emergency-maintenance.html">Emergency guidance</a></div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</ResidenceLayout>
